{
  "case_id": "2017-16-498",
  "document_hash": "d2bfd8ec1de7aece7713602823af6baba7a0e1ad7bd89ec5063d9ee0baef20ea",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Scott E. Gant",
      "case_id": "2017-16-498",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d2bfd8ec1de7aece7713602823af6baba7a0e1ad7bd89ec5063d9ee0baef20ea",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d2bfd8ec1de7-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Section 2(b) of the Gun Lake Act is unconstitutional because it is incompatible with several well-established strands of this Court's separation-of-powers jurisprudence as well as with Article III itself. With Section 2(b), Congress directed the federal courts to dismiss a pending case otherwise properly before the courts."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2017-16-498",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d2bfd8ec1de7aece7713602823af6baba7a0e1ad7bd89ec5063d9ee0baef20ea",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d2bfd8ec1de7-0000-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Chief Justice Roberts: We'll hear argument this morning in Case 16-498, Patchak versus Zinke."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2017-16-498",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d2bfd8ec1de7aece7713602823af6baba7a0e1ad7bd89ec5063d9ee0baef20ea",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d2bfd8ec1de7-0000-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Mr. Gant, when -- when you say \"directed that a case shall be dismissed,\" are you referring only to the last few words of this statute or are you referring more broadly?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Scott E. Gant",
      "case_id": "2017-16-498",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d2bfd8ec1de7aece7713602823af6baba7a0e1ad7bd89ec5063d9ee0baef20ea",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d2bfd8ec1de7-0000-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 10,
        "start": 10
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The rule -- the rule, I submit, the Court should adopt is if a statute is properly -- deemed as properly -- is properly construed as a jurisdiction-stripping statute, it is still subject to separation-of-powers analysis."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2017-16-498",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d2bfd8ec1de7aece7713602823af6baba7a0e1ad7bd89ec5063d9ee0baef20ea",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d2bfd8ec1de7-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "If this suit had proceeded to a conclusion, would -- and Patchak prevailed, would he be entitled to costs?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2017-16-498",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d2bfd8ec1de7aece7713602823af6baba7a0e1ad7bd89ec5063d9ee0baef20ea",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d2bfd8ec1de7-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: What's the case?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2017-16-498",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d2bfd8ec1de7aece7713602823af6baba7a0e1ad7bd89ec5063d9ee0baef20ea",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d2bfd8ec1de7-0002-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "those are the two cases that Petitioner cites in his opening brief. One is Sebelius, which is the claims processing rule, and then Arbaugh, which is the -- the elements of a cause of action."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2017-16-498",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d2bfd8ec1de7aece7713602823af6baba7a0e1ad7bd89ec5063d9ee0baef20ea",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d2bfd8ec1de7-0002-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 48,
        "start": 48
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The APA doesn't apply if another statute precludes judicial review."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Federal Court Scholars",
      "case_id": "2017-16-498",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d2bfd8ec1de7aece7713602823af6baba7a0e1ad7bd89ec5063d9ee0baef20ea",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d2bfd8ec1de7-0002-0005",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 59,
        "start": 59
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the line that the other side has offered in the Federal Court Scholars amicus brief supporting the other side, and this is at page 15 of that amicus brief. It says -- and this is relying on Professor Hart, it says, \"It is one thing to exclude completely the federal courts from adjudication; it is quite another to vest the federal courts with jurisdiction to adjudicate but simultaneously restrict the power of those courts to perform the adjudicatory function in the manner they deem appropriate.\""
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice KAGAN",
      "case_id": "2017-16-498",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d2bfd8ec1de7aece7713602823af6baba7a0e1ad7bd89ec5063d9ee0baef20ea",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d2bfd8ec1de7-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 69,
        "start": 69
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Is that constitutional?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "House of Representatives",
      "case_id": "2017-16-498",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d2bfd8ec1de7aece7713602823af6baba7a0e1ad7bd89ec5063d9ee0baef20ea",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d2bfd8ec1de7-0003-0001",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 74,
        "start": 74
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Or, as the House of Representatives argued on pages 3 and 20 of its brief, what 2(a) -- 2(b) does is it implements 2(a)."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Heritage Reporting Corporation",
      "case_id": "2017-16-498",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d2bfd8ec1de7aece7713602823af6baba7a0e1ad7bd89ec5063d9ee0baef20ea",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d2bfd8ec1de7-0003-0003",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 74,
        "start": 74
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "when the plaintiff gets kicked out of court, they have lost."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Federal Respondents",
      "case_id": "2017-16-498",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d2bfd8ec1de7aece7713602823af6baba7a0e1ad7bd89ec5063d9ee0baef20ea",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d2bfd8ec1de7-0003-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 75,
        "start": 75
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Respondents -- Federal Respondents said they didn't know quite what some of the provisions in the Gun Lake Act means except they do know that it prevents Mr. Patchak's case from going forward."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Heritage Reporting Corporation",
      "case_id": "2017-16-498",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d2bfd8ec1de7aece7713602823af6baba7a0e1ad7bd89ec5063d9ee0baef20ea",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d2bfd8ec1de7-0003-0004",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 76,
        "start": 76
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The case is submitted."
    },
